# UPSTREAM NOTE
# This patch should be contributed upstream to rmohr/bazeldnf.
#
# The problem: bazeldnf's lock file URL template system constructs URLs as
#   base_url + "/" + relative_path
# for each mirror listed under a repository entry. This works fine for multiple
# mirrors of the same CDN/mirror structure, but cannot accommodate a fallback
# to a content-addressed store (like GCS builddeps) where the URL path is just
# the sha256 hash rather than the same relative RPM path.
#
# The fix: add a "fallback_urls" field to individual RPM entries in the lock
# file. These are full pre-formed URLs appended to the mirror-constructed list,
# allowing Bazel to fall back to them natively (ctx.download tries each URL
# in order).
#
# This pattern is needed by KubeVirt and likely any project that:
#   1. Pulls RPMs from a rolling upstream (CentOS Stream) that supersedes old
#      package versions (causing 404s on the mirror URLs), AND
#   2. Mirrors those RPMs to a content-addressed immutable store (GCS builddeps)
#      as a stable fallback.
#
# Upstream PR: TODO - open PR against https://github.com/rmohr/bazeldnf
